19:   - UI interaction\n1020: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n1021:   - Mobile responsiveness\n1022:   - Touch interaction\n1023:   - Audio on different browsers\n1024:   - Performance with high cell counts\n1025:   - Accessibility testing\n1026: \n1027: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1028: \n1029: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n1030: \n1031: - [ ] Write README.md\n1032:   - Project overview\n1033:   - Installation instructions\n1034:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n1035:   - Configuration options\n1036:   - Known issues and limitations\n1037: - [ ] Add code comments\n1038:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n1039:   - State machine logic\n1040:   - Performance-critical sections\n1041: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n1042:   - Component props\n1043:   - Utility functions\n1044:   - Configuration schemas\n1045:   - Type definitions\n1046: - [ ] Create developer guide\n1047:   - Architecture overview\n1048:   - How to add new features\n1049:   - Debugging tips\n1050:   - Common patterns\n1051: - [ ] Document expert settings\n1052:   - Each parameter explanation\n1053:   - Recommended values\n1054:   - Impact on gameplay\n1055: \n1056: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1057: \n1058: ---\n1059: \n1060: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1061: \n1062: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1063: \n1064: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1065: \n1066: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1067: \n1068: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1069: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1070: \n1071: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1072: \n1073: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1074: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1075: \n1076: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1077: \n1078: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1079: \n1080: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1081: \n1082: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1083: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1084: \n1085: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1086: \n1087: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1088: \n1089: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1090: \n1091: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1092: \n1093: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1094: \n1095: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1096: \n1097: ---\n1098: \n1099: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1100: \n1101: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1102: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1103: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1104: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1105: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1106: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1107: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1108: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1109: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1110: \n1111: ## Testing Milestones:\n1112: \n1113: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1114: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1115: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1116: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1117: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1118: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1119: \n1120: ## Success Criteria:\n1121: \n1122: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1123: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1124: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1125: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1126: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1127: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1128: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1129: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1130: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1131: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1132: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1133: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1134: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1135: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1136: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1137: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1138: \n1139: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1140: \n1141: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1142: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1143: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1144: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1145: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1146: \n1147: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1148: \n1149: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1150: \n1151: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1152: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1153: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1154: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1155: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1156: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1157: \n1158: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1159: \n1160: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1161: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1162: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1163: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1164: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1165: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1166: \n1167: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n1168: \n1169: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n1170: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n1171: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n1172: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n1173: \n1174: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n1175: \n1176: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n1177: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n1178: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n1179: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n1180: \n1181: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n1182: \n1183: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n1184: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n1185: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n1186: \n1187: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n1188: \n1189: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n1190: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n1191: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n1192: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n1193: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n1194: \n1195: ## Notes:\n1196: \n1197: - Update status (checkmark) as tasks are completed\n1198: - The plan is prioritized: CRITICAL first, then HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW\n1199: - Parallel tracks enable concurrent work where dependencies allow\n1200: - Focus on MVP first, then incrementally add polish\n1201: - src/lib/ is project's standard library for shared utilities\n1202: - Prefer consolidated implementations in src/lib/ over ad-hoc copies\n1203: - Always run lint and typecheck commands after completing features\n1204: - Test on both desktop and mobile throughout development\n1205: - Gather user feedback during development to improve UX\n1206: - Document decisions and trade-offs in comments or docs\n1207: - Keep code modular and maintainable for future enhancements\n1208: \n1209: ## Recent Progress:\n1210: \n1211: **Turn Summary (Sprint 2.5 & 2.4 Integration - Game Component Scoring Integration):**\n1212: \n1213: - Integrated movement detection and scoring into Game.tsx simulation loop\n1214: - Added automatic simulation stepping during RUNNING phase (was missing before)\n1215: - Implemented handleSimulationStep callback that:\n1216:   - Steps the simulation using stepSimulation()\n1217:   - Detects connected components using findConnectedComponents()\n1218:   - Tracks clusters across generations using trackClusters()\n1219:   - Calculates score based on cluster classifications using calculateGenerationScore()\n1220:   - Updates all state appropriately (scoreState, trackedClusters, previousScore)\n1221: - Added useEffect that runs simulation loop during RUNNING phase at 200ms intervals\n1222: - Integrated ScoreDisplay component into Game UI at top-left position\n1223: - Added score state management (scoreState, previousScore)\n1224: - Added trackedClusters ref to avoid re-render issues\n1225: - Score now updates in real-time during simulation\n1226: - Score resets on Clear/Random/phase transitions appropriately\n1227: - ScoreDisplay shows smooth increment animations and milestone flashes\n1228: - Added imports for movement detection, scoring, ScoreDisplay components\n1229: - Updated Game.tsx with proper state and callback management\n1230: - All tests passing (240 total)\n1231: - Type checking passes\n1232: - Lint passes for modified files\n1233: \n1234: **Technical Decisions:**\n1235: \n1236: - Simulation runs at 200ms intervals during RUNNING phase via setInterval in useEffect\n1237: - Movement detection uses BFS for cluster finding (findConnectedComponents)\n1238: - Scoring uses cluster classifications: MOVER (10pts), OSCILLATOR (2pts), STATIC (0pts)\n1239: - ScoreDisplay shows smooth animations (lerp 0.2s) and milestone flashes (every 100 points)\n1240: - Tracked clusters stored in ref (trackedClusters) to avoid re-render issues\n1241: - previousScore state tracks previous score for ScoreDisplay animations\n1242: - Score resets on Clear/Random handle functions and phase transitions\n1243: - handleSimulationStep callback integrates all three systems: simulation → movement → scoring\n1244: - Phase-based cleanup: score and tracked clusters reset when phase changes\n1245: \n1246: **Turn Summary (Sprint 2.5 - Scoring System):**\n1247: \n1248: - Implemented scoring.ts library with per-generation scoring logic\n1249: - Implemented calculateGenerationScore for scoring clusters by classification (MOVER: 10pts, OSCILLATOR: 2pts, STATIC: 0pts)\n1250: - Implemented score multiplier support with rounding\n1251: - Implemented score capping at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER to prevent overflow\n1252: - Implemented score state management (currentScore, generationScore, totalPatternsTracked)\n1253: - Implemented resetScore for clean level transitions\n1254: - Implemented formatScore for display with K/M suffixes\n1255: - Implemented milestone detection in 100-point increments\n1256: - Added comprehensive test suite with 21 tests\n1257: - All tests passing (205 total, up from 157)\n1258: - Type checking and linting passing\n1259: - Scoring system now complete and integrated into Game component\n1260: - Scoring system integrated with movement detection for real-time score updates (240 total tests passing)\n1261: \n1262: **Technical Decisions:**\n1263: \n1264: - Score capped at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (9,007,199,254,740,991) for safety\n1265: - Multiplier applied before rounding using Math.round for fair fractional scoring\n1266: - FormatScore uses K/M suffixes: 1000 = \"1.0K\", 1000000 = \"1.0M\"\n1267: - Milestone detection every 100 points for achievement feedback\n1268: - Score state immutable (returns new state objects)\n1269: - No score carryover between levels (reset to 0 on level start)\n1270: \n1271: **Turn Summary (Sprint 2.4 - Movement Detection):**\n1272: \n\n(Output truncated at 51200 bytes. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 1272)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation Plan\n\nThis plan prioritizes building a playable, enjoyable game first, then incrementally enhances with advanced features. All requirements from 14 specification files are included with proper dependencies and priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Sprint 1: Foundation (MVP Core)\n\n_Goal: Basic Game of Life with visualization, interaction, and game flow_\n\n### 1.1 Project Setup & Build System (CRITICAL - FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- [x] Choose and initialize framework (React/Vite recommended for performance) - React + Vite initialized\n- [x] Initialize TypeScript project with strict mode - tsconfig.json created with strict mode\n- [x] Configure Vite build system - vite.config.ts configured\n- [x] Set up ESLint and Prettier - eslint.config.js and .prettierrc.json created\n- [x] Create project structure:\n  - src/components/ - React components\n  - src/lib/ - Shared utilities and core logic\n  - src/types/ - TypeScript type definitions","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771181916592,"end":1771181916633}}}}
