{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771181953431,"sessionID":"ses_39d54d119ffe5wknN3nwR32dw0","part":{"id":"prt_c62ab5d01001wuG2B5KUvtBG58","sessionID":"ses_39d54d119ffe5wknN3nwR32dw0","messageID":"msg_c62ab42bd001fJq7JlkNCRZwh4","type":"tool","callID":"call_568a460d7ac844e8b82fe978","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Study specs/* files","prompt":"Study all 13 spec files in the specs/ directory and provide a comprehensive summary of:\n1. What each spec file covers\n2. The overall application architecture and features\n3. Key requirements and constraints\n4. Integration points between systems\n\nRead these files:\n- specs/audio-sonification.md\n- specs/auto-advance-transitions.md\n- specs/canvas-rendering.md\n- specs/expert-settings.md\n- specs/flux-management.md\n- specs/grid-interaction.md\n- specs/level-progression.md\n- specs/movement-detection.md\n- specs/phase-management.md\n- specs/scoring-system.md\n- specs/simulation-engine.md\n- specs/ui-overlay.md\n- specs/user-interaction.md\n\nProvide a structured summary organized by functional areas."},"output":"task_id: ses_39d54a3a4ffetjsRVEjsJU8jNo (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Game of Life Specification Summary\n\nBased on all 13 spec files, here's a structured analysis organized by functional areas:\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Each Spec File Covers\n\n### Core Simulation & Rendering\n- **simulation-engine.md**: Conway's Game of Life rules implementation, toroidal boundaries, cell age tracking, double-buffer rendering, neighbor counting algorithm\n- **canvas-rendering.md**: Dark neon theme rendering, age-based color gradients, glow effects, responsive cell sizing (18px mobile/20px desktop), DPR scaling, intensity metrics\n\n### Game Mechanics\n- **phase-management.md**: Three-phase state machine (PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED), countdown system, phase transitions, timer management\n- **flux-management.md**: Resource system for cell placement, 1 Flux per cell cost, refund mechanism in planning phase, strategic allocation decisions\n- **level-progression.md**: Progressive difficulty scaling, time limits increase per level (45s base + 15s increments), auto-advance transitions, cumulative scoring\n- **scoring-system.md**: Real-time points based on pattern classification (Movers: 10pts/gen, Oscillators: 2pts/gen), multiplier support, high score persistence\n\n### Interaction Systems\n- **grid-interaction.md**: PLANNING phase cell placement/removal, minimum 1 cell to start, coordinate mapping, visual cursor feedback\n- **user-interaction.md**: Mouse and touch input handling, draw/erase modes, coordinate conversion, prevent default behaviors, drag support\n\n### Pattern Analysis\n- **movement-detection.md**: Connected component detection with 8-connectivity, centroid tracking, cluster classification (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC), velocity calculation\n\n### Audio\n- **audio-sonification.md**: Web Audio API integration, generation sounds (pitch mapped to row position), interaction sounds (draw/erase tones), volume/waveform controls\n\n### Transitions\n- **auto-advance-transitions.md**: Cinematic fade sequences (2s fade out, 2s interstitial, 2s fade in), skip mechanism (Space/ESC), state management during transitions\n\n### UI/Configuration\n- **ui-overlay.md**: Cinematic intro with glitch effect, glass HUD controls, settings panel, phase status display, responsive design\n- **expert-settings.md**: Hidden configuration panel, tunable parameters (movement detection, scoring, level generation), localStorage persistence, export/import JSON\n\n---\n\n## 2. Overall Application Architecture\n\n### Phase-Based State Machine\n```\nPLANNING (unlimited time, full cell manipulation)\n    ↓ [START button]\nCOUNTDOWN (3-2-1, no input)\n    ↓\nRUNNING (timed, add-only cell placement)\n    ↓ [Timer=0 or all cells dead]\nFINISHED (2s pause, view-only)\n    ↓ [Auto-advance]\nPLANNING (next level, fresh start)\n```\n\n### Core Data Flow\n```\nUser Input → Grid Interaction → Simulation Engine → Pattern Detection → Scoring System\n                                              ↓\n                                       Canvas Rendering\n                                              ↓\n                                       Audio Sonification\n```\n\n### Key Features\n1. **Strategic Resource Management**: Players allocate Flux between planning and running phases\n2. **Pattern-Based Scoring**: Incentivizes creating moving patterns (gliders, spaceships) over static structures\n3. **Progressive Difficulty**: Each level increases time limits, encouraging more complex patterns\n4. **Real-Time Audio Feedback**: Birth events mapped to pitch based on spatial position\n5. **Cinematic Transitions**: Smooth fade sequences between levels with skip support\n6. **Responsive Design**: Mobile-optimized (18px cells) and desktop (20px cells) layouts\n7. **Expert Tuning**: Hidden dev panel for balancing parameters without code changes\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Requirements and Constraints\n\n### Technical Constraints\n- **Performance**: Movement detection must process 50-200 clusters in <16ms (60fps target)\n- **Grid Sizes**: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n- **Canvas Scaling**: Must handle DPR (devicePixelRatio) for sharp rendering\n- **Audio Policy**: AudioContext requires user gesture to initialize (browser autoplay restriction)\n- **State Consistency**: Flux updates must be atomic with cell placement to prevent race conditions\n\n### Gameplay Constraints\n- **Flux Limits**: Default 20 Flux per level, no carryover between levels\n- **Phase Restrictions**: No cell removal during RUNNING phase (add-only)\n- **Minimum Cells**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- **Auto-Advance**: FINISHED phase auto-transitions after 2.0s (non-interactive)\n- **No Lose Condition**: Game always advances; only score accumulation varies\n- **Toroidal Boundaries**: Grid wraps on all edges (pac-man style)\n\n### UI/UX Requirements\n- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44×44px for mobile accessibility\n- **Transition Durations**: 2.0s fade out, 2.0s interstitial, 2.0s fade in (all skippable)\n- **Skip Mechanism**: Space/ESC skips transitions at any point\n- **Browser Tab**: Timer continues during inactive tab during gameplay, pauses during transitions\n\n### Browser Compatibility\n- **Required APIs**: Web Audio API, HTML5 Canvas, requestAnimationFrame\n- **Platform Support**: Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge), iOS with gesture requirement\n- **Accessibility**: Reduced motion preference support for transitions\n\n---\n\n## 4. Integration Points Between Systems\n\n### Data Integration Matrix\n\n| Source System | Target System | Data/Events Shared |\n|---------------|---------------|-------------------|\n| **Simulation Engine** | Movement Detection | Grid state, birth statistics |\n| **Simulation Engine** | Canvas Rendering | Cell ages, grid dimensions |\n| **Simulation Engine** | Audio Sonification | Born count, average row position |\n| **Simulation Engine** | Scoring System | Grid state (for pattern analysis) |\n| **Movement Detection** | Scoring System | Cluster classifications (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC) |\n| **User Interaction** | Simulation Engine | Cell placement/removal coordinates |\n| **User Interaction** | Audio Sonification | Draw/erase interaction events |\n| **User Interaction** | Flux Management | Cell placement cost tracking |\n| **Flux Management** | Grid Interaction | Available Flux for placement validation |\n| **Phase Management** | All Systems | Current phase state, transition events |\n| **Phase Management** | UI Overlay | Phase display, timer/visibility control |\n| **Level Progression** | Phase Management | Level transitions, time limits |\n| **Level Progression** | Flux Management | Initial Flux allocation per level |\n| **Level Progression** | Scoring System | Cumulative score tracking across levels |\n| **Expert Settings** | Movement Detection | centroidHistoryLength, movementThreshold |\n| **Expert Settings** | Scoring System | moverPointsPerGeneration, scoreMultiplier |\n| **Expert Settings** | Level Progression | baseTimeSeconds, timeIncrementPerLevel |\n| **Expert Settings** | Canvas Rendering | mobileCellSize, desktopCellSize |\n| **UI Overlay** | All Systems | Speed, grid size, audio enabled, grid lines settings |\n| **Auto-Advance Transitions** | Phase Management | Transition state (FADING_OUT/INTERSTITIAL/FADING_IN/READY) |\n| **Auto-Advance Transitions** | Level Progression | Level advancement trigger |\n| **Canvas Rendering** | UI Overlay | Intensity metric (for ambient effects) |\n\n### Critical State Dependencies\n\n1. **Phase Locking**: \n   - Grid interaction only enabled during PLANNING\n   - Running phase only allows cell addition (no removal)\n   - FINISHED phase is read-only\n\n2. **Flux Coordination**:\n   - Must validate Flux availability before cell placement\n   - Refund mechanism only active in PLANNING phase\n   - Flux resets per level (no carryover)\n\n3. **Simulation Timing**:\n   - Simulation speed controlled via UI settings\n   - Generation triggers: movement detection, scoring, audio\n   - Timer independent of simulation speed\n\n4. **Audio Lazy Initialization**:\n   - AudioContext created on first user interaction\n   - Must resume if suspended\n   - Disabled state returns early without sound generation\n\n5. **Transition State Machine**:\n   - Auto-advance has 5 states: PLAYING → FADING_OUT → INTERSTITIAL → FADING_IN → READY\n   - Skip mechanism can jump to READY from any state\n   - Simulation continues hidden during fade out\n\n### Event Flow Examples\n\n**Cell Placement Flow:**\n```\nUser clicks canvas → User Interaction (coordinate conversion) → \nGrid Interaction (Flux validation) → Simulation Engine (grid update) → \nCanvas Rendering (redraw) + Audio Sonification (draw sound) → \nMovement Detection (recompute clusters on next tick) → \nScoring System (potential future points)\n```\n\n**Level Completion Flow:**\n```\nTimer reaches 0 → Phase Management (RUNNING → FINISHED) → \nScoring System (finalize score) → Auto-Advance Transitions (2s FINISHED display) → \nFading Out (2s) → Interstitial (2s, load next level) → \nFading In (2s) → READY → Phase Management (PLANNING next level) → \nFlux Management (reset to 20) + Simulation Engine (clear grid)\n```\n\n**Pattern Scoring Flow:**\n```\nSimulation Engine (generation step) → Movement Detection (connected components) → \nCentroid Tracking (calculate velocity) → Classification (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC) → \nScoring System (apply points: Mover=10, Oscillator=2) → UI Overlay (display score)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a sophisticated Game of Life variant that transforms the classic cellular automaton into a strategic game with:\n\n1. **Resource constraints** (Flux system) that force players to plan carefully\n2. **Pattern-based incentives** that reward creating dynamic, moving structures\n3. **Progressive difficulty** that scales time limits across levels\n4. **Multi-sensory feedback** (visual, audio) that enhances engagement\n5. **Developer-friendly tuning** via expert settings for balancing\n6. **Cinematic polish** with smooth transitions and responsive UI\n\nThe architecture is well-separated into functional modules with clear integration points, using React state management with refs for performance-critical operations (simulation, canvas rendering).\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs/* files","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d54a3a4ffetjsRVEjsJU8jNo","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771181923588,"end":1771181953429}}}}
